# `graft`, not `[tool.setuptools.package-data]` globs, because the vendored trees
# are third-party content whose shape this repo does not control.
#
# package-data patterns are expanded with Python's `glob`, which cannot see
# dot-prefixed names. `agents/**/*` alone ships 65 of the 66 files and silently
# drops `agents/configs/workmux/.workmux.yaml` — the only file
# `install-config workmux` copies. Adding `agents/**/.*` recovers dot-prefixed
# *files*, but `**` still does not descend into a dot-prefixed *directory*, so a
# skill that grows a `.github/` or `.claude/` upstream loses its contents the
# same way and no finite set of globs closes that off.
#
# `graft` walks with `os.walk` and filters nothing, so the whole class is covered
# rather than the two instances a glob pair reaches. Verified against a wheel
# built from a tree carrying a dot-prefixed subdirectory: 67 files with `graft`,
# 66 with the globs, mode 100755 preserved on all five scripts either way.
#
# `include_package_data` defaults to true under pyproject metadata, which is what
# carries these into the wheel and not only the sdist.
graft wfctl/agents
graft wfctl/specify
